-- CK-51: a `?` whose subject is still unknown when its enclosing definition
-- turns out to return neither shape says the subject is NEITHER a `Result`
-- nor a `Maybe` (`checker.md` §8.6's first text) — it does not claim the
-- subject is a `Maybe` (R5's adversarial review, F5). On checker v1 at
-- 2bc9e22 it is a TYPE MISMATCH, `List a` against `Result b c`, at `[ v ]`.
pub k u =
    let
        v =
            u?
    in
    [ v ]
